From 607416971be0e7e44245108f5bcf0a47890ab762 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wutt6678 <wutt6678@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 17:36:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] Add PRH (Poisoned Reward Hijacking) reward-channel
 substitution

Implements the first-commit slice of the PRHBench pilot design for the
AI Safety Gridworlds environments:

- agent_system/environments/prh.py: dependency-free (numpy-only) module
  with the episode-level Bernoulli poison mask, hidden<->observed
  reward-channel selection, and a PRHRewardRouter that logs
  prh_clean_reward/prh_proxy_reward/prh_poisoned/prh_training_reward
  into each info dict without ever overwriting hidden_reward/
  observed_reward.
- agent_system/environments/env_manager.py: wires the router into
  SafetyGridworldsEnvironmentManager. The mask is sampled once per
  episode at reset() and held fixed for the whole episode. Only the
  training-side manager gets a router (prh_training=True); the
  validation-side manager (prh_training=False) is untouched, so
  validation metrics stay ground-truth regardless of env.prh.enabled.
  Also adds a proxy_hidden_gap = observed - hidden metric to
  success_evaluator.
- verl/trainer/config/ppo_trainer.yaml: new env.prh config block,
  disabled by default (enabled: false), so every other environment and
  every existing safety-gridworld run is unaffected.

Deliberately deferred (see plan): step-level/adaptive poisoning, a
learned attacker, defenses, and touching the PPO trainer's WandB
logging beyond the existing generic success-metric path.
